ree hours and then  you get to walk the palace and kind of  you know feel like what it must have  been like back then  so it's kind of like an immersive  theater experience and it's wonderful to  see  everybody dressed in costume i think i  was there at that palace i'm pretty sure  it's the same palace  yeah it's a pretty famous palace i kind  of like where everyone goes when you  visit korea  so when i was visiting korea i stayed at  the westin chosen which is really close  and easy to get to to kyongbokung palace  and i mean the rooms are spacious the  amenities the lobby's gorgeous and it's  just so nice to just  be a tourist all day and then come back  to kind of luxurious hotel settings and  just like  rest relax rejuvenate and then go back  out and just you know  see the rest of seoul so for uh my dance  for cambodian dance  um it used to be performed in front of  like kings and queens and royalty where  people would  um be dressed in in similar outfits to  like the cambodian wedding outfits but  they would be  like in golds with like brackets and  with crowns  but they would do special hand movements  so there's hand movements that correlate  with the dance and  the hand movements like mean something  so there's definitely a lot of  movement and storytelling and it's slow  like watching it like a ballet where you  can actually see the story which is a  lot about like  life and balance and i was never  able to like get it like perfectly  because just like it's really technical  and you have to bend your fingers and  like they practice  betting their fingers as a kid so they  like  they can like bend it all the way back  like i don't know if you can try it but  it's it's really intense  yeah like it gets it tells the story so  switzerland is very much  known for the alporn or in swiss it's  called alpol  which is basically the same um and it's  used or used to be used  um back in the day in the alps in the  swiss alps where you know they have cows  and sheep  and they used a horn to call them so  that they would come all back together  and go back to the stables at night  and it doesn't have any buttons or any  strings or any openings it's just a  solid  wooden corn and i've never played it  myself but i know you caroline have  but i know it's very difficult to play  it that was difficult but after  like practicing it's like once you get  it you just don't want to stop  [Music]  [Applause]  debbie you have to do it you have to do  it the next time you go  yes i want to next time whenever i can  go back home  it's going to be on my list for sure i  actually want to go to switzerland  uh i want to go to all of your countries  but switzerland i have ties to somewhat  because  my mom is half swiss my mom is half  nigerian  yeah so she she tells me stories all the  time of like how she would go there for  um holiday when she was young but i've  never been able to go  so hearing all of your stories i'm like  yes have to get there and if you're like  us i know you can't wait until we can  travel again to experience  these and other music theater and dance  performances in person  [Music]  you
 

